@Andrzej

“Whiff” is classic (American) slang for swinging and missing a baseball or tennis ball. Whiff means a puff of air, so when you swing hard and miss, all that results is a puff of air. 

Square meal is a full meal (like dinner, breakfast, lunch), as opposed to a snack or quick bite. Value meal is a classic fast-food term—lots of food, supposedly not too expensive. Classic McDonald’s term.

@MB
@Francis

OK, I was unfamiliar with that meaning of whiff. And while I knew value meal, square meal I think I've never seen before, or at least I didn't remember it if I saw it.

Thank you!

